.TH HEERC 5 "2026-09-01" "HEE" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
heerc \- per-operator shell environment for the HEE toolchain
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ~/git/human-execution-engine/tooling/heerc
.SH DESCRIPTION
A POSIX shell fragment sourced by the operator's
.BR bash (1)
startup, deliberately minimal: it makes bare
.B hee
resolve, and carries per-operator display preference. It is not a general
dotfile \(em aliases, prompt and other opinion stay in personal dotfiles.
.PP
Sourced from dotfiles'
.I .bashrc
behind an existence guard, so an operator using dotfiles without this repo
cloned is unaffected.
.SH WHAT IT DOES
.TP
.B PATH bootstrap
Prepends
.I ~/.local/bin
if absent. Real trigger, 2026\-08\-26: PATH resolution depended on one
operator's personal dotfiles happening to add that directory, and broke for
a fresh homedir and for any other identity.
.TP
.B Governance reminder
Prints a one\-line reminder to read
.IR prompts/PROMPTING_RULES.md .
Real footgun, 2026\-08\-28: a session ran mutating git across three repos
before reading rule 1 (never push directly to main).
.SH VARIABLES
.TP
.B HEE_STATUS_STYLE
Status rendering for every HEE tool:
.BR icon " (default), " ascii ", " plain .
See
.BR hee-status (7).
Per\-operator preference, which is why it lives in an rc file rather than
being hardcoded.
.SH NOT SET HERE
Runtime variables consumed by individual tools \(em
.BR HEE_REPO_DIR ", " HEE_CRED_PASS ", " HEE_DERIVED_DIRS
\(em are passed per invocation or by the calling tool, not declared here.
This file stays PATH\-and\-preference only.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hee (1),
.BR hee-status (7)
